---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getSite } from '../lib/site';

const { contactEmail } = getSite();
---
<Layout
  title="Terms of service"
  description="Terms governing use of the Bycon marketing website. Product terms are set in your separate agreement."
>
  <article class="prose" style="max-width: 42rem;">
    <h1>Terms of service (website)</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      Last updated: April 29, 2026. These terms apply to this marketing site. Use of the Bycon TMS or other paid services is
      governed by your order form and applicable agreement—not by this page alone.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptance</h2>
    <p>
      By accessing <strong>bycon.com</strong> (and related marketing pages), you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do
      not use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Use of the site</h2>
    <p>
      You may browse and use contact links for lawful business purposes. You may not attempt to disrupt the site, probe
      systems without authorization, scrape in violation of our robots policy (if any), or misuse any contact channels.
    </p>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      Content on this site (text, branding, layout) is owned by Bycon or used with permission. You may not copy or reuse it
      for commercial purposes without prior written consent, except as allowed by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      This site is provided “as is.” Descriptions of products and roadmaps are informational and may change. We disclaim
      warranties to the extent permitted by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, Bycon is not liable for indirect or consequential damages arising from your
      use of this marketing site, or for any loss arising from reliance on site content.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware, USA, excluding conflict-of-law rules, unless a
      different governing law is mandatory where you reside.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms:{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
